# Calendar App Architecture

A self-contained, client-only calendar built with React + Material Design 3 web components.

## File Structure


client/
├── pages/
│   └── Index.tsx                       # Root page — wraps CalendarLayout + CalendarApp
├── components/
│   └── calendar/
│       ├── CalendarLayout.tsx          # Context provider + seed data + CRUD handlers
│       ├── Sidebar.tsx                 # Left nav: Create button, MiniCalendar, nav items
│       ├── MiniCalendar.tsx            # Compact monthly grid for sidebar date selection
│       ├── MonthView.tsx               # Full monthly grid (7-col, event chips, overflow)
│       ├── WeekView.tsx                # 7-col time grid with absolute-positioned events
│       ├── DayView.tsx                 # Single-column time grid with absolute events
│       ├── EventCard.tsx               # Small event chip used in MonthView cells
│       └── EventDialog.tsx             # md-dialog for creating / editing events
└── types/
    └── calendar.ts                     # CalendarEvent, ViewMode, EventColor types


## State Management

All shared state lives in `CalendarLayout.tsx` via React Context (`CalendarContext`):

| State | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `selectedDate` | `Date` | Currently focused date (drives all views) |
| `viewMode` | `ViewMode` | `'month' \| 'week' \| 'day'` |
| `events` | `CalendarEvent[]` | All calendar events (in-memory, seeded) |

Access state anywhere inside `<CalendarLayout>` with `useCalendar()`.

## Types (`client/types/calendar.ts`)

```ts
type ViewMode = "month" | "week" | "day";
type EventColor = "primary" | "secondary" | "tertiary";

interface CalendarEvent {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  date: string;       // "YYYY-MM-DD"
  startTime: string;  // "HH:MM" (24h)
  endTime: string;    // "HH:MM" (24h)
  color: EventColor;
  description?: string;
}
```

## Event Colors

Events cycle through 3 MD3 color roles:
- `primary` → `--md-sys-color-primary-container` / `--md-sys-color-on-primary-container`
- `secondary` → `--md-sys-color-secondary-container` / `--md-sys-color-on-secondary-container`
- `tertiary` → `--md-sys-color-tertiary-container` / `--md-sys-color-on-tertiary-container`

## Time Grid Layout (WeekView / DayView)

- `HOUR_HEIGHT = 60px` (WeekView) / `64px` (DayView) per hour
- Events positioned with `position: absolute; top: (startMin/60)*HOUR_HEIGHT`
- Height = `((endMin - startMin) / 60) * HOUR_HEIGHT`
- Current time indicator uses `--md-sys-color-error` (red line)

## Key Interactions

| Action | Component | Handler |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| Click day cell in MonthView | `MonthView` | Navigates to DayView for that date |
| Click "+N more" | `MonthView` | Navigates to DayView |
| Click empty time slot | `WeekView` / `DayView` | Opens create dialog pre-filled with date+time |
| Click event chip | Any view | Opens edit dialog |
| Click "Create" in sidebar | `Sidebar` | Opens blank create dialog |
| Click mini-calendar date | `MiniCalendar` | Updates `selectedDate` |

## View Switcher (TopBar tabs row)

`TopBar` returns a React fragment with two elements:

1. `<header>` — the main nav bar (hamburger, logo, today/prev/next, date label, search, settings, avatar)
2. A `<div>` containing `<md-tabs>` with four `<md-primary-tab>` children (Day / Week / Month / Schedule)

The tabs row sits directly below the header and carries the `borderBottom` separator.

**Sync pattern** — `activeTabIndex` is derived from `VIEWS.findIndex(v => v.id === viewMode)` so
it stays in sync whenever viewMode changes from any source (mini-calendar, keyboard shortcuts, etc.).
Tab interactions fire a native `"change"` event; a `useEffect` listener reads `event.detail.index`
(or `el.activeTabIndex` as fallback) and calls `setViewMode(VIEWS[idx].id)`.

The old custom dropdown (`viewDropdownOpen` state + click-outside effect + dropdown JSX) has been
removed entirely.

## MD3 Components Used

- `md-dialog` — EventDialog modal
- `md-filled-text-field` — event form inputs
- `md-filled-button` / `md-text-button` — dialog actions
- `md-icon-button` / `md-icon` — nav arrows, close, hamburger
- `md-outlined-button` — "Today" button in top bar
- `md-divider` — sidebar section separator
- `md-tabs` / `md-primary-tab` — view switcher row in TopBar

## No Backend

Events are stored in React state only. Page refresh resets to seed data.
To persist events, add localStorage in CalendarLayout (useEffect + JSON.stringify).
